<FeatureFacts id="coach-programs" />

## Your programs, LogIt's and the community's

Coaching › Programs has three lists. **Yours** are the programs you made or copied, each with
how many clients have it. **LogIt** has LogIt's own programs, and **Community** has program packs
from the plugin directory. Those two are read-only: Start from a program shows one with its days,
and Copy to my programs makes it yours to change. A newer version of a pack never changes your
copy, or your clients'.

## Build a program

<HowTo id="studio.program" />

Changes save as you go, so leaving the page loses nothing. If the same program is open on another
device, changes to different things come across by themselves with a note; only when both changed
the same exercise does LogIt ask which to keep. Programs made before the builder whose weeks have
different exercises are still edited week by week.

## Rules

A rule decides how the numbers move from week to week. Pick one for the whole program at the
top of the builder, and a different one for any exercise from its settings. LogIt Adaptive,
Linear, the 4-week wave and Fixed are built in. Programs › Rules is where you make your own,
with the same builder lifters have on the phone: where the weight comes from (strength estimate,
last session or a wave), the rep range, reps left, the set layout, the step, what happens on a
stall, the number of sets and whether to hold in a calorie deficit. "What it would do" shows the
numbers on a client's lift, and "In words" is what clients see under "Why this weight?". Your
programs follow changes to a rule; clients' copies follow when you update them.

A client's copy can follow its own rule: ⋯ › Change their rule… on their Training tab. Clients'
phones work out each week's numbers from their own lifts when they start the day. Programs ›
Rules also has what clients can swap to.

## Swaps

What clients can swap to is in Programs › Rules: any exercise, the same main muscles, or only the
swaps you list on each exercise. On the phone, after a swap they choose just today or for the rest
of the program, with a reason if they like; the rest of the program tells you, and later days start
with the swap. On their Training tab, Keep it changes their copy to match, and Put it back… puts the
original back and tells them. A message asking about a swap has "Swap an exercise in their
program…" on its menu, to change it in their copy straight from the conversation. Whatever your
rule, "Do something else today" is always there for them; it logs as a swap you can see.

## Every week

See every week shows what the rule plans for each exercise, week by week. On a client's copy the
numbers come from their own strength estimates, and weeks they've done show what they did; on your
own program the rule is said in words ("6–8 reps, from their estimate") until you pick a client
under Showing to preview it with their lifts.

- **LogIt Adaptive** picks the weight from their estimate for the reps, leaving two in the tank.
- **Linear** adds a rep a week through the range, then the step (+2.5 kg) and back to the bottom.
- **4-week wave** runs 5s, 3s and 5/3/1 off a training max, then a light week.
- **Fixed** keeps the numbers as you typed them.
- **Lighter weeks** have about half the sets, at the bottom of the range and the same weight.

Double-click a cell, or press Enter, to type over it, like `62.5 × 7`; it stays put whatever the
rule does, with a blue edge. Clear gives it back to the rule. Copy, paste and Fill to the end of
the block (up to the next lighter week) are on the cell's menu.

## Give it to a client

<HowTo id="studio.assign" />

From a program, or from a client's page, Assign gives one or several clients their own copy. It
starts when they tap Start on their phone, or on a date you choose. Someone already on a program
can switch now, or start the new one the day theirs ends. A program with a block from a plugin
says so: without the plugin on their phone, that block shows as a note and the rest of the day
works.

On a client's Training tab, their program is at the top: which week they're in, its rule, the
next lighter week, this week's days and what they've done, and any swaps. Their main lifts show
their best set this week, their strength estimate then and four weeks ago, and what the program
plans next time. ⋯ on the program has Change program… and Stop the program.

